      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "This diagram presents Phase 3 of OCF device integration: how a locally onboarded device is joined to the SmartThings Cloud. It demonstrates\nhow a Mediator (the mobile app) acts as a trust bridge to provision cloud credentials to the device, allowing the device to maintain its own long-\nlived connection to the cloud.\n\nArchitectural Participants\n    1. Mediator: The SmartThings mobile app.\n    2. Auth Provider: Samsung Account OAuth 2.0 authorization server.\n    3. OCF Cloud: Cloud IoT Gateway and Resource Directory (/oic/rd).\n    4. OCF Device: The physical appliance (already owned locally).\n\nStep-by-Step Walkthrough\n    Phase 1: Mediator Sign-In & Delegation\n        Steps 1-2: The app completes an OAuth 2.0 authorization code flow with the Samsung Account service and receives an access token.\n        Steps 3-4: The app calls the OCF Cloud to register the device's di (Device ID) under the user's account and requests a one-time device\nauthorization code / token (at).\n    Phase 2: Mediator Provisions Device over Local DTLS\n        Step 5: The app talks to the device over the secure local DTLS channel and updates the resource /oic/r/coapcloudconf:\n            cis: OCF Cloud address (coaps+tcp://...)\n            sid: Cloud UUID\n            at: One-time access token / authorization code\n            apn: Authorization provider name (\"samsung\")\n            Device state shifts to cps: readytoregister.\n     Phase 3: Device Connects Direct to OCF Cloud\n        Step 6: The device opens an outbound TCP connection to the cloud endpoint and negotiates TLS using its factory-burned manufacturer\ncertificate and ALPN.\n        Steps 7-8 (/oic/sec/account): Device sends a CoAP POST to /oic/sec/account with its di and the one-time token at. The cloud registers\nthe device, returning a permanent user ID (uid), device access token, and refresh token.\n        Steps 9-10 (/oic/sec/session): Device initiates a session by posting to /oic/sec/session (login: true). The cloud confirms the active\nsession.\n        Steps 11-12 (/oic/rd Publish & Observe): Device publishes all its observable application resources (/switch/0, /temperature/0, /oic/d,\n/oic/p) to the Cloud Resource Directory. The cloud issues a CoAP GET with the Observe option (RFC 7641) to subscribe to real-time state\nchanges.\n        Steady State (Step 13): The device maintains the TCP connection using application-layer CoAP Ping/Pong and automatically refreshes\ntokens via POST /oic/sec/tokenrefresh before expiry.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "This diagram presents Phase 3 of OCF device integration: how a locally onboarded device is joined to the SmartThings Cloud. It demonstrates how a Mediator (the mobile app) acts as a trust bridge to provision cloud credentials to the device, allowing the device to maintain its own long-lived connection to the cloud.\n\nArchitectural Participants\n    1. Mediator: The SmartThings mobile app.\n    2. Auth Provider: Samsung Account OAuth 2.0 authorization server.\n    3. OCF Cloud: Cloud IoT Gateway and Resource Directory (/oic/rd).\n    4. OCF Device: The physical appliance (already owned locally).\n\nStep-by-Step Walkthrough\n    Phase 1: Mediator Sign-In & Delegation\n        Steps 1-2: The app completes an OAuth 2.0 authorization code flow with the Samsung Account service and receives an access token.\n        Steps 3-4: The app calls the OCF Cloud to register the device's di (Device ID) under the user's account and requests a one-time device authorization code / token (at).\n    Phase 2: Mediator Provisions Device over Local DTLS\n        Step 5: The app talks to the device over the secure local DTLS channel and updates the resource /oic/r/coapcloudconf:\n            cis: OCF Cloud address (coaps+tcp://...)\n            sid: Cloud UUID\n            at: One-time access token / authorization code\n            apn: Authorization provider name (\"samsung\")\n            Device state shifts to cps: readytoregister.\n     Phase 3: Device Connects Direct to OCF Cloud\n        Step 6: The device opens an outbound TCP connection to the cloud endpoint and negotiates TLS using its factory-burned manufacturer certificate and ALPN.\n        Steps 7-8 (/oic/sec/account): Device sends a CoAP POST to /oic/sec/account with its di and the one-time token at. The cloud registers the device, returning a permanent user ID (uid), device access token, and refresh token.\n        Steps 9-10 (/oic/sec/session): Device initiates a session by posting to /oic/sec/session (login: true). The cloud confirms the active session.\n        Steps 11-12 (/oic/rd Publish & Observe): Device publishes all its observable application resources (/switch/0, /temperature/0, /oic/d, /oic/p) to the Cloud Resource Directory. The cloud issues a CoAP GET with the Observe option (RFC 7641) to subscribe to real-time state changes.\n        Steady State (Step 13): The device maintains the TCP connection using application-layer CoAP Ping/Pong and automatically refreshes tokens via POST /oic/sec/tokenrefresh before expiry.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
